"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nHumans do not live to be happy, but are just designed to feel happiness \nto survive.  \nHappiness is a survival tool, not a purpose.\n\nActually, it's a fact I knew but wanted to ignore.  \nThe means and the purpose have been swapped.\nIt's a slightly uncomfortable truth I learned through .\n\nIt was interesting that there are separate genetic temperaments that have a huge impact on happiness.  \nExtroverted people feel  in the process of meeting and hanging out with people itself, and that this is a social animal and this is essential for survival, it was perhaps natural.  \n\nI agree that happiness is about frequency, not intensity.  \nHumans quickly get used to any positive event and happiness is quickly reset.  \nThis is also designed for survival.\n\nSmall but certain happiness (So-hwak-haeng) is actually not small, but certain happiness.  \n"